extraction_notes: "WB30 D-Bees of North America printed 213-215 (cache p214-p216, cache page = printed + 1); every number read off a 200 dpi render. Heading Vintex Warriors - Optional Player Character or NPC, printed 214. || CATEGORY: a race with its own skills that takes no O.C.C. (printed O.C.C.s: they do NOT select an O.C.C.). mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || XP: the Note says use the same Experience Table as the Military Specialist. The catalog holds no Rifts Military Specialist ladder (geofront-military-specialist is the Japan class of that name, a different book and table; the hu- rows are Heroes Unlimited), so no xp_table is stored. Copy that ladder here if a Rifts Military Specialist is imported. || M.D.C.: 6D6 + P.E., plus 2D6 per level starting at level one, stored as mdc_base. P.S. 3D6+11 is Augmented; Spd 3D6+13 (average 22). Horror Factor not applicable. P.P.E. 2D6+5. || BONUSES: +1 attack per melee, +1 initiative, +3 strike, +1 parry and dodge, +3 disarm, +1 entangle, +4 pull punch, +1 roll with impact, +3 vs Horror Factor as printed. Impervious to most diseases is a total immunity, left in prose rather than a save bonus. The tail''s +2 strike and +1 parry are conditional and are ability text. || SKILLS: catalog base plus printed bonus: Literacy: Native Language 40+10, Climbing 40+15, Land Navigation 36+10, Math: Basic (catalog Mathematics: Basic) 45+12, Military Etiquette 35+20, Radio: Basic 45+15, Rope Works 30+15 (printed (15%), read as a bonus), Sign Language 25+10, Swimming 50+15. Acrobatics, Boxing and Combat Driving carry no bonus. Language: Native (+4%, American adopted) is Language: Native Tongue at 98; the +4% would exceed 98 and is a note. Pilot: Vehicle of choice (+12%) is a choice from Pilot with bonus 12. W.P. Ancient three and W.P. Modern two are choices from the ancient and modern W.P. rows (W.P. Rope is granted by name, so it is left out of the ancient list). Superior Aim''s automatic Targeting is the printed W.P. Targeting. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts or Commando, pick one, is a choice; no upgrade price is printed, so no hand_to_hand block. || AREA OF SPECIALTY: takes the place of related skills; five skills from any ONE of the listed categories at +15%. Stored as occ_related_skills count 5 with every listed category at bonus 15; the one-category rule cannot be enforced and is a restriction line. Physical: None and Pilot Related: None are omitted. Pilot excludes Submersible, Tanks, Robot and Power Armor skills, stored as an except list of the matching Pilot rows. W.P. carries no bonus (a W.P. has no percentage). || SECONDARY: two at each of levels 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 and 11. || EQUIPMENT: set of clothing, leather boots (boots), leather gloves (gloves), backpack, bedroll, two canteens, 1D4 pens or markers (marker x1D4), pocket mirror, wooden cross, language translator (portable-language-translator), satchel (purse-satchel, the row an earlier import used for a satchel). E-Clips 1D6+3 for each W.P. weapon are stored as one e-clip x1D6+3 (the per-weapon count is in GM Notes). Not stored, no catalog row or no named item: suit of medium or non-environmental armor (4D6+40 M.D.C.), one weapon for each W.P., 1D4 pieces of white chalk, a can of spray paint, notebook and personal items. || MONEY: 1D6x1,000 credits in trade goods or Black Market items. || NOT STORED: size 6-7 feet, weight 200-250 pounds, life span 6D6+99 years, slave market value 1D4x10,000, allies, enemies and habitat are GM Notes."
